{"base_rate":0.48079470198675495,"brier":0.17644900662251656,"bss":0.29316112188677124,"bss_hi":0.40349789288196813,"bss_lo":0.18900688393289525,"chart":{"base":[685.4,61.3],"fp":[300.1,294.4],"lead":"62,253.9 272,246.7 482,235.1 692,222","note":{"base":"skill 0.29 — higher than 53% of cities","fp":"low end +10pp, high end +17pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 53% of cities","rel":"promised 7% → rained 16%; promised 96% → rained 80%"},"rel":"107.8,398.8 461.5,258.9 669,119.8"},"country":"AU","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.12905960264900662,"ess":325.8965803844239,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Sunshine Coast</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Sunshine Coast rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>85%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(1%), there is still roughly a <b>12%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 755 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMAROOCHYDORE AERO, 6.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.29, ranked 101 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(55&ndash;153) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>12%</b></td><td class='num'>224</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>24%</td><td class='num'><b>27%</b></td><td class='num'>78</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>74%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>85%</b></td><td class='num'>227</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Sunshine Coast</b> <span class=\"muted\">Australia</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.29</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>55&ndash;153\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>755 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Sunshine Coast &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Sunshine Coast\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-a